          "confidence": "reviewed",
          "notes": "Free French National Committee (CNF) organized by Charles de Gaulle on 24 September 1941, according to official French National Assembly. It exercised provisional public powers for Free France/France combattante and represented Free French authorities, without claiming that Vichy was a legitimate Republic cabinet. It was absorbed into the French Committee of National Liberation created on 3 June 1943. End 2 June 1943 is the ATLAS last-full-day before successor context begins, not independent evidence of exact legal extinguishment at midnight. Free France's 18 June 1940 appeal and preceding Free French military activity are NOT retroactively treated as 1941 CNF government."
