          "notes": "CFLN instituted in Algiers by joint de Gaulle-Giraud ordinance 3 June 1943. It coordinated the armed and civil Free French and North African liberation authorities, was initially co-chaired by Charles de Gaulle and Henri Giraud, and was renamed Gouvernement provisoire de la République française on 3 June 1944. 2 June 1944 is the last full day before that name transition (ATLAS convention). This government context concerns resistance/liberation provisional authority and asserts no parallel sovereign French country, no recognition of Vichy as legitimate Republic government, and no unregistered Persons or Activity creation."
